Lint warns when an acceptance check reads like a question
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
hug task lint flags an acceptance check that is really a question to a person. [1mToday a check like[0m
[1m'Should the ASKED row show the count?' sits among the checks, is easy to tick by mistake, and[0m
[1mnobody is asked, so the question waits for someone to notice it and turn it into a hug task ask,[0m
[1mwhich in practice happens late or never.[0m The finding names the check, and its fix: line runs hug
task ask with the check's text.

PURPOSE
Jørgen 2026-11-19 08:55Z: questions today look like acceptance criteria. A question belongs
where a person is asked and answers it.

PRINCIPLE
Lint finds, it never rewrites a check. One finding per check, with one fix: line.

ACCEPTANCE
  ☐ 1. A check that ends in '?' is a lint finding, with a fix: line that runs hug task ask (test)





